    "title": "Free Trial - Apple TV Guide - IGN",
    "text": "There are various Apple TV subscription plans and bundles to choose from, but if you just want to give the service a test drive, there are options available to you. Unlike other major streaming services, Apple TV still offers a free trial to new subscribers. You can also get the service for free a few different ways. Apple TV Free Trials7-Day Free TrialApple TV+ Free TrialIf you haven't subscribed to Apple TV before, you can try out the service free for seven days. This free trial is available to anyone, but still requires a valid email and credit/debit card. Once the free trial ends you'll automatically pay the full $12.99 monthly subscription fee and be set up to automatically renew. You can cancel the service any time before those seven days are up to avoid any charges. 1-Month Free Trial with Apple OneIf you're looking for a slightly longer free trial, you can get a full month for free by trying out Apple One. This is Apple's full suite of services and will also get you access to things like Apple Music, Apple Arcade, and Apple News. You still need to be a new or returning subscriber to each of the included services to get the the free trial. So if you already have an Apple TV subscription, you won't be able to include that in your free month. 3-Month Free Trial with New DeviceThe overall best Apple TV free trial is the one you get when you purchase a new Apple device. New subscribers can get three months of the service for free after purchasing any eligible Apple product. This includes iPhones, iPads, Macs, or Apple TV devices. Both Apple Watches and AirPods are excluded from this list. This offer is only good for the first 90 days after the new device is activated. Was this guide helpful?In This Guide",
